<title>RUSSIA: Russia Jan-Apr non-CIS oil exports up 11 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Russia Jan-Apr non-CIS oil exports up 11 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian exports of crude oil outside the Commonwealth of Independent States (CIS) rose 11 percent in the first four months of 1997 over the same year-ago period to 34.8 million tonnes (2.09 million barrels per day), the State Statistics Committee said on Thursday.</p>
<p>It said oil product exports were 17.7 million tonnes during the first four months of the year, 31 percent ahead of the same period in 1996.  </p>
<p>Non-CIS natural gas exports from January to April edged down two percent year-on-year to 43.5 billion cubic metres.</p>
<p>The committee it gave the following figures --</p>
<p>	    RUSSIA JAN-APRIL 1997 NON-CIS ENERGY EXPORTS</p>
<p>				    Jan-April	 pct change from</p>
<p>					1997	     Jan-April 1996</p>
<p> crude oil (million tonnes)	 34.8		    +11</p>
<p> oil products (million tonnes)    17.7		    +31</p>
<p>natural gas</p>
<p>  (billion cubic metres)	    43.5		     -2</p>
<p>-- Moscow Newsroom +7095 941 8520</p>
